
================================================================================================
ARITHMETIC IDENTITIES AND WHAT THEY ARE ALLOWED TO FORGET
================================================================================================
checked n<= 80, q<=24 for Ramanujan formula
  tau=sigma0     mismatches=[]
  sum phi        mismatches=[]
  phi=mu*id      mismatches=[]
  psi=id*|mu|    mismatches=[]
  sum J2         mismatches=[]
  ramanujan      mismatches=[]

Guardrail reading:
  tau/sigma forget residue order and phase; use them only for divisor-size capacity.
  phi/Jordan retain primitive unit capacity; use them for exact-period resource counts.
  psi retains squarefree plus-support; use it as a support capacity, not as a route label.
  Ramanujan c_q keeps the primitive cyclotomic shell but still forgets endpoint owners.

