Readout: scalar channels are features, not proof quotients, whenever they mix routes.
The guarded packet signature is intentionally over-labelled; its job is to say what
has not yet been proved safe to forget.

================================================================================================
TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS ON QUOTIENT CHANNELS
================================================================================================
vertices:
  raw_divisor_counts: keeps=factor exponents; tau/sigma capacity
    forgets=unit residues; primitive phase; endpoint owners; route labels
  squarefree_psi_support: keeps=radical support; plus squarefree capacity
    forgets=prime powers; unit residues; endpoint owners; signs
  totient_jordan_unit_capacity: keeps=primitive exact-period counts; CRT unit capacity
    forgets=unit arrangement; endpoint owners; K33/petal route labels
  gcd_strata: keeps=which divisors of q each speed hits; imprimitive/unit split
    forgets=cyclic phase inside each stratum; endpoint owners
  ramanujan_primitive_shell: keeps=primitive cyclotomic phase by q; orthogonal shell projection
    forgets=individual primitive residues; endpoint owners; state-lift debt
  exact_period_packet: keeps=q/Farey predicate; unit residues; Ramanujan shell
    forgets=continuous endpoint order unless attached; proof-family names
  labelled_lrc_packet_sheaf: keeps=q/Farey; Haar open/boundary; endpoint owners; C27/K33/state labels; dual certificates
    forgets=raw runner names when irrelevant

score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1}
directed_3_cycles=0
Hamiltonian path:
  labelled_lrc_packet_sheaf > exact_period_packet > ramanujan_primitive_shell > gcd_strata > totient_jordan_unit_capacity > squarefree_psi_support > raw_divisor_counts

Assumption challenge:
  considered vertices: runners, residues, divisors, unit twists, gcd strata,
    primitive Fourier modes, endpoint owners, C27/K33 packets, and proof obligations.
  chosen vertices here: quotient channels.
  preserved predicate: whether a channel retains enough payload to support the next
    LRC implication without silently mixing AP/GW, q-witness, K33, petal, and covering routes.
  destroyed information: raw runner identity when it is not part of the next predicate.

================================================================================================
HYP-2978 PROOF TARGET
================================================================================================
Ramanujan-divisor admissibility theorem target:

  A quotient Q used in an LRC14 proof step is admissible only if every
  coordinate it forgets is one of:
    (1) invariant under the step's allowed moves;
    (2) reconstructible from retained q/Farey, unit, gcd, and Ramanujan data;
    (3) annihilated by a proved orthogonality or dual certificate; or
    (4) placed in an explicit residual bucket with endpoint/state-lift labels.

Concrete LRC14 route:
  Use divisor/totient/Jordan/psi data as capacity ledgers.
  Use Ramanujan c_q profiles as primitive-shell Fourier guards.
  Then hand off to HYP-2974/2977 harmonic duals or HYP-2965/2969 endpoint
  packets before claiming that a qdiv>14 zero-open packet cannot exist.

Most important new falsifier:
  two rows sharing a scalar divisor/Ramanujan signature but taking different
  LRC proof routes.  The audit already exhibits this for qdiv/open-state/
  residue-shell quotients, so those channels must remain labelled features,
  not final proof quotients.
